hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18134","Yahya ibn Saeed narrated to us, Abdullah narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Saeed al-Qattan narrated to me, he said: My father narrated to us, and Yahya ibn Main narrated to me, he said: Yahya ibn Saeed narrated to me, from Abu Jafar al-Khatmi who said: Umarah ibn Khuzaymah and al-Harith ibn Fudayl narrated to me, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Abi Qurad who said: I went out with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on pilgrimage, and I saw him come out from the privy, so I followed him with a water skin or a cup, and sat waiting for him on the road; and when he relieved himself, he would go far."
